# Human Interface Guidelines (cross-platform web)

Source: [Apple HIG](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/) — **cross-platform rules only** (no watchOS/tvOS/visionOS/CarPlay-specific guidance).

This is a **web app**. Apply HIG *intent* with CSS/HTML on all platforms. Do not ship Apple-only fonts, SF Symbols as a font, or APIs that fail off Safari.

**Always use shared primitives** — never one-off buttons, spinners, or settings rows per page.

## Shared components (required)

| Need | Use | Never |
|------|-----|-------|
| Button | `Button` | raw `<button>` without `hit-min` / `hit-expand` |
| Icon-only control | `IconButton` (requires `aria-label`) | unlabeled icon `<button>` |
| Dense inline icon | `IconButton size="compact"` | `IconButton` default (44×44 **drawn**) in chips/chat |
| Hub navigation | `HubTab`, `HubTabIconButton`, `BottomHubBar` | per-page tab markup |
| Loading (page/section) | `LoadingState`, `PageLoading`, `ListLoadingSkeleton` | `Loader2` / blank screens |
| Auth layout gate | `LayoutGate` | `return null` while loading |
| Settings toggle | `SwitchRow` | bare `Switch` without row label |
| Form field | `FormField` + `formFieldControlProps` | placeholder-only inputs |
| RHF forms | `Form`, `FormLabel`, `FormControl` | ad-hoc labels |
| Selection list row | `SelectionRow` | tiny checkbox/switch rows |
| Empty content | `EmptyState` (`page-layout`) | custom empty divs |
| Page structure | `PageShell`, `NavPageHeader`, `PageSection` | ad-hoc `page-container` wrappers; nested `home-flow` / `stack-gap-*` for header-to-body; `PageHeader` / `NavPageHeader` `description` |
| Destructive confirm | `AlertDialog` (Cancel + destructive) | `window.confirm`, popover with only Delete |

## Hit target ≠ visual size (critical)

The 44×44px rule is the **tappable region**, not the drawn control. Apple: if a control looks smaller, **expand the hit area around the visual** — do not enlarge the glyph, chip, or chrome.

| Context | Drawn size | Hit | Primitive |
|---------|------------|-----|-----------|
| Toolbar, hub, back, composer send/attach, form submit, list-row edit | 44×44 | same | `IconButton` / `Button` default |
| Chat react / reply / delete, reaction pills, chip remove | ~20–32px | visual size; keep on **one row** | `IconButton size="compact"`, `Button size="chip"` — **no** `.hit-expand` |

- `.hit-min` — the **box** is ≥44px (toolbars, list rows). Never on chips or per-message actions.
- `.hit-expand` — visual stays as styled; `::before` expands tap area to 44px. **Only where controls are spaced apart** (toolbars, form rows). Never on stacked chat reactions/actions — the overlays overlap the row above/below.
- Crowding a message with three 44px **drawn** buttons, or overflowing 44px hit overlays onto reaction chips, violates **simplicity** and **don’t crowd**. Compact visual **without** vertical overflow is the correct HIG reading in dense threads.

```tsx
// ✅ Toolbar / composer
<IconButton aria-label="Send" icon={ArrowUp} />

// ✅ Dense inline (chat, chips)
<IconButton size="compact" aria-label="Reply in thread" icon={CornerUpLeft} />
<Button size="chip" variant="ghost">👍 2</Button>

// ❌ Never — inflates layout
<IconButton aria-label="Reply" icon={CornerUpLeft} /> // default 44×44 under every message
<Button className="hit-min">👍</Button>
```

## Design principles

Full guidance: **human-centered-design** (structure, flow, continuity, IA, progressive disclosure, and each principle in detail). Here: component-level defaults only.

## Layout

- Group related content with space, surfaces, or separators.
- Essential info first; align; **don’t crowd**.
- Content may bleed to edges; **controls stay inset**.
- Respect `env(safe-area-inset-*)`.
- Phone: primary actions in thumb reach. Desktop: denser OK; hit still ≥44px (may overlap).
- Adapt to resize; don’t lock `maximum-scale`.

### Page rhythm (required)

Every route shares one vertical rhythm — **never** nest extra wrappers to “fix” spacing between the page title and body.

| Layer | Use | Gap |
|-------|-----|-----|
| Route shell | `PageShell` (or `page-container`) | `gap-5` between **direct children** |
| Page title | `NavPageHeader`, `PageHeader`, or `home-greeting` | `.page-header` inset only — no extra margin below |
| Body (multiple grouped sections) | `page-flow` on the body block | `gap-5` between sections |
| Grouped section | `HomeGroupedSection` | `gap-1.5` eyebrow → card (internal) |

```tsx
// ✅ Hub / grouped page — header and body are siblings in PageShell
<PageShell>
  <NavPageHeader action={…} />
  <ReadingPlanOverview … />
</PageShell>

// ✅ Home — same shell, greeting is the page title
<PageShell>
  <HomeGreeting … />
  <HomeBibleSection … />
</PageShell>

// ❌ Nested rhythm wrapper (causes inconsistent header-to-body gap)
<PageShell>
  <div className="home-flow">
    <NavPageHeader />
    <Body />
  </div>
</PageShell>

// ❌ Ad-hoc spacing on the shell
<div className="page-container space-y-8">…</div>
```

## Typography

- System font stack only (never embed SF/NY).
- Body ≥ 16px; avoid Ultralight/Thin.
- Scale with `rem` / `--app-font-size-scale`.
- Inputs on touch: **16px minimum** (prevents iOS zoom).
- Caption/meta can be smaller but keep contrast (7:1 if small).

## Color and appearance

- Semantic colors; same color = same meaning.
- Never color-only — pair with text or icon.
- Destructive = red (`variant="destructive"`), never primary/accent.
- Light **and** dark; default follows **OS** (`system`).
- Contrast ≥ 4.5:1 (7:1 small text). Honor `prefers-contrast: more` and `prefers-reduced-transparency`.
- Translucency needs opaque fallback (`.ui-scrim` / solid background).

## Controls

- Hit region **≥ 44×44 px** — see table above. Press/`active` + `:focus-visible` ring.
- One prominent **filled** button per view (the most likely action). Secondary = ghost/outline.
- Destructive is never the default/Return/focused action.
- Icon-only: `aria-label` required (`IconButton` enforces).
- Give visible press feedback; don’t rely on hover alone (hover-reveal stays visible on coarse pointers).

## Alerts and destructive actions

- Use `AlertDialog` for irreversible work (delete message, leave group).
- Title + short message explaining the consequence.
- Two actions: **Cancel** (focused, outline) and the destructive action (red, not default).
- Never a popover whose only button is Delete.
- Don’t use alerts for inline validation — show the error next to the field.

## Motion and input

- Honor `prefers-reduced-motion` (no scale/hover zoom: use `motion-safe:`).
- Hover-reveal stays visible on coarse pointers (`.hover-reveal`).
- `touch-action: manipulation` on interactive elements (already on `Button`).

## Loading

- **Skeletons over blank screens** — `LoadingState variant="skeleton"`, `ListLoadingSkeleton`, `PageLoading`.
- **Defer spinners** — `useDeferredLoading` / `LoadingState` (~400ms).
- **Announce state** — `role="status"`, `aria-live="polite"`, `aria-busy`.
- **Don’t block unnecessarily** — shell first; inline/section loading for partial content.
- **Determinate progress** — `Progress` when duration known.
- **Empty ≠ loading** — never show empty states while `isLoading`.

## No header subtitles

`NavPageHeader` and `PageHeader` are **title only** — do not pass `description` or add a subtitle paragraph directly under the page title.

- Section headings farther down the page (`PageSection`, `h2` / `h3`, tabs, cards) are fine.
- **OK:** dialog titles, empty-state copy, list row titles, tab labels, form field labels.

## Selection and input

- **Visible labels** — `FormField`, `FormLabel`; never placeholder-only forms.
- **Touch targets** — `SwitchRow`, `SelectionRow` for toggles/checkboxes.
- **Keyboard** — `focus-visible` rings; logical tab order; Enter submits single-purpose forms.
- **Mobile keyboards** — `type`, `inputMode`, `autoComplete` on `Input`.
- **Validation** — `aria-invalid`, `aria-describedby`; destructive + message text.
- **Pickers** — `SelectItem` rows ≥ 44px; checkmark for selected.

## Patterns (cross-platform)

- **Feedback** — Accessible status; alerts for critical info only; confirm irreversible loss.
- **Entering data** — Prefer choices over typing; validate inline; secure fields for secrets.
- **Loading** — Show something immediately; let people use the app while content loads.
- **Modality** — Modal only with clear benefit; obvious dismiss; confirm before data loss.
- **Onboarding** — Teach through interaction; keep brief; optional tutorials.
- **Searching** — Primary position when important; show scope; respect privacy.
- **Settings** — Sensible defaults; minimal options; respect system settings.
- **Undo/redo** — Predictable, visible results; support multiple undo when feasible.
- **Notifications** — Accurate urgency; don’t over-notify.
- **Accounts** — Delay sign-in; explain benefits; minimal data collection.
- **Menus** — Related secondary actions can share a menu instead of a row of large always-visible buttons.

## Accessibility (cross-platform)

- Perceivable, operable, understandable — not color-only, sufficient contrast.
- Support larger text / zoom.
- Labels for all controls; errors in text.
- Keyboard and screen-reader paths for core tasks.

```tsx
// ✅ Always
<PageShell>
  <NavPageHeader />
  {children}
</PageShell>
<HubTab active={active} label="Events" icon={Calendar} onClick={…} />
<SwitchRow id="anon" label="Post anonymously" checked={v} onCheckedChange={setV} />
<LayoutGate loading={loadingAuth} ready={!!user}>{children}</LayoutGate>
<LoadingState isLoading={loading} variant="skeleton">{content}</LoadingState>
<FormField id="email" label="Email" error={err}>
  <Input {...formFieldControlProps('email', err)} />
</FormField>
<IconButton size="compact" aria-label="Add reaction" icon={SmilePlus} />

// ❌ Never
<button className="h-8 w-8">…</button>
<IconButton aria-label="Reply" icon={CornerUpLeft} /> // default size under a chat bubble
if (loading) return null;
<Switch id="x" /> without visible label row
```
